Outside it is cold.
The bags are very heavy.
I walk slowly home.
I stop once to rest my arms.
Finally, I am home in my flat.
I carry the bags out into the kitchen.
I put most of the food away.
I put the milk into the fridge.
But the bread and the cheese stay on the table.
I am hungry.
I would like some food now.
I look at my kitchen.
It is not empty anymore.
The fridge and the cupboards are full.
Now it is truly my home.
I am very proud.
